{
 "_doc": "Rosace face feature library at 144 px (head 25 px skull top to chin). Authored pixel data, one character per pixel; tools/art-construct/face_construct.py places these on the construction grid (docs/character/ART-RULES.md section 6) and tunes them with parameters (gaze, eye row, brow raise, mouth corner, highlight placement). Eye symbols: O = upper lash (OL), '~' = eye opening (the tool fills it with the iris and the white from the gaze parameter), L = lower-lash dot (I3), G = Ignited glow (A4), '.' = leave the skin. Brow symbols: '#' = brow pixel (the tool draws OL where it lands on hair, I3 on skin). Mouth, blush and nose grids use the palette KEY in tools/art-construct/artlib.py (m = S4, t = S3, p = SB, w = W1). Facing: authored for a head turned screen-right (three-quarter), so the near eye is on the left with its outer end on the left, and the far eye is on the right with its outer end on the right. Front view: 'front' is the screen-left eye; the screen-right eye is its mirrored shape, then the iris, white and highlight are redone by the tool (ART-RULES FC-N02). Rows run top to bottom; 'row0' is the first row's height above the lash-top row (the lash-top row = 0). 'box' = [first column, width] of the eye box inside the grid (the flick may sit outside it). Every grid is [I]: a first authored value, checked by rules_check.py and changed through the learning log.",
